{"headword":"רָצַח","parent_lexicon":"BDB Dictionary","content":{"senses":[{"definition":"<strong>vb. murder, slay (</strong>NH (rare, also in deriv.) = BH; cf. Arabic <span dir=\"rtl\">رَضَحَ</span>, <span dir=\"rtl\">رَضَخَ</span> <em>break, bruise, crush</em><strong>)</strong>;—"},{"senses":[{"definition":"Pf. 3 ms. consec. <span dir=\"rtl\">זְר׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Numbers 35:27\" href=\"/Numbers.35.27\">Nu 35:27</a>, <span dir=\"rtl\">וּרְצָחוֹ</span> <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 22:26\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.22.26\">Dt 22:26</a>; 2 ms. <span dir=\"rtl\">(הֲ)רָצַחְתָּ</span> <a data-ref=\"I Kings 21:19\" href=\"/I_Kings.21.19\">1 K 21:19</a>; Impf. 3 ms. <span dir=\"rtl\">יִרְצַח</span> <a data-ref=\"Numbers 35:30\" href=\"/Numbers.35.30\">Nu 35:30</a>; <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 4:42\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.4.42\">Dt 4:42</a>; 2 ms. <span dir=\"rtl\">(-צַח) תִּרְצָ֑ח</span> <a data-ref=\"Exodus 20:13\" href=\"/Exodus.20.13\">Ex 20:13</a> = <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 5:17\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.5.17\">Dt 5:17</a>; inf. abs. <span dir=\"rtl\">רָצֹחַ</span> <a data-ref=\"Hosea 4:2\" href=\"/Hosea.4.2\">Ho 4:2</a>; <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 7:9\" href=\"/Jeremiah.7.9\">Je 7:9</a>; Pt. act. <span dir=\"rtl\">רֹצֵחַ</span> <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 19:3\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.19.3\">Dt 19:3</a> +, <span dir=\"rtl\">רוֹ׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 4:42\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.4.42\">4:42</a> +;—<em>murder, slay</em>, with premeditation, <a data-ref=\"Exodus 20:13\" href=\"/Exodus.20.13\">Ex 20:13</a> (E) = <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 5:17\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.5.17\">Dt 5:17</a>; <a data-ref=\"Hosea 4:2\" href=\"/Hosea.4.2\">Ho 4:2</a>; <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 7:9\" href=\"/Jeremiah.7.9\">Je 7:9</a>; <a data-ref=\"I Kings 21:19\" href=\"/I_Kings.21.19\">1 K 21:19</a> (all abs.); c. acc. pers. <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 22:26\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.22.26\">Dt 22:26</a>, unawares <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 4:42\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.4.42\">Dt 4:42</a>; <em>slay</em> as avenger <a data-ref=\"Numbers 35:27\" href=\"/Numbers.35.27\">Nu 35:27</a>, <a data-ref=\"Numbers 35:30\" href=\"/Numbers.35.30\">30</a> (P; ‖ <span dir=\"rtl\">הֵמִית</span> v <a data-ref=\"Numbers 35:19\" href=\"/Numbers.35.19\">19</a>, <a data-ref=\"Numbers 35:21\" href=\"/Numbers.35.21\">21</a>); especially pt. as subst. = <em>slayer, manslayer</em>, without intent, <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 4:42\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.4.42\">Dt 4:42</a>; <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 19:3\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.19.3\">19:3</a>, <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 19:4\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.19.4\">4</a>, <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 19:6\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.19.6\">6</a>; also in P: <a data-ref=\"Numbers 35:6\" href=\"/Numbers.35.6\">Nu 35:6</a>, <a data-ref=\"Numbers 35:11\" href=\"/Numbers.35.11\">11</a>, <a data-ref=\"Numbers 35:12\" href=\"/Numbers.35.12\">12</a>, <a data-ref=\"Numbers 35:25\" href=\"/Numbers.35.25\">25</a>, <a data-ref=\"Numbers 35:26\" href=\"/Numbers.35.26\">26</a>, <a data-ref=\"Numbers 35:27\" href=\"/Numbers.35.27\">27</a>, <a data-ref=\"Numbers 35:28\" href=\"/Numbers.35.28\">28</a>; <a data-ref=\"Joshua 20:3\" href=\"/Joshua.20.3\">Jos 20:3</a>, <a data-ref=\"Joshua 20:5\" href=\"/Joshua.20.5\">5</a>, <a data-ref=\"Joshua 20:6\" href=\"/Joshua.20.6\">6</a>; <a data-ref=\"Joshua 21:13\" href=\"/Joshua.21.13\">21:13</a>, <a data-ref=\"Joshua 21:21\" href=\"/Joshua.21.21\">21</a>, <a data-ref=\"Joshua 21:27\" href=\"/Joshua.21.27\">27</a>, <a data-ref=\"Joshua 21:32\" href=\"/Joshua.21.32\">32</a>, <a data-ref=\"Joshua 21:26\" href=\"/Joshua.21.26\">26</a> (van d. H., Baer, v <a data-ref=\"Joshua 21:33\" href=\"/Joshua.21.33\">33</a> Gi; all P); <em>murderer</em>, with intent, <a data-ref=\"Numbers 35:16\" href=\"/Numbers.35.16\">Nu 35:16</a><sup>(×2)</sup>, <a data-ref=\"Numbers 35:17\" href=\"/Numbers.35.17\">17</a><sup>(×2)</sup>, <a data-ref=\"Numbers 35:18\" href=\"/Numbers.35.18\">18</a><sup>(×2)</sup>, <a data-ref=\"Numbers 35:19\" href=\"/Numbers.35.19\">19</a>, <a data-ref=\"Numbers 35:21\" href=\"/Numbers.35.21\">21</a><sup>(×2)</sup>, <a data-ref=\"Numbers 35:30\" href=\"/Numbers.35.30\">30</a>, <a data-ref=\"Numbers 35:31\" href=\"/Numbers.35.31\">31</a>; also <a data-ref=\"Job 24:14\" href=\"/Job.24.14\">Jb 24:14</a>."}],"form":"Qal"},{"senses":[{"definition":"Impf. 1 s. <span dir=\"rtl\">אֵרָצֵחַ</span> <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 22:13\" href=\"/Proverbs.22.13\">Pr 22:13</a> <em>I shall be slain;</em> Pt. fs. as adj. <span dir=\"rtl\">אִשָּׁה הַנִּרְצָחָה</span> <a data-ref=\"Judges 20:4\" href=\"/Judges.20.4\">Ju 20:4</a> <em>the murdered woman</em>."}],"form":"Niph."},{"senses":[{"definition":"(intens.) <em>murder, assassinate:</em> 3 mpl. <span dir=\"rtl\">יְרַצְּחוּ</span> <a data-ref=\"Hosea 6:9\" href=\"/Hosea.6.9\">Ho 6:9</a> (abs.), <span dir=\"rtl\">יְרַצֵּ֑חוּ</span> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 94:6\" href=\"/Psalms.94.6\">ψ 94:6</a> (acc. pers., ‖ <span dir=\"rtl\">הָרַג</span>); <a data-ref=\"Psalms 62:4\" href=\"/Psalms.62.4\">ψ 62:4</a> v. infr.; Pt. <span dir=\"rtl\">מְרַצֵּחַ</span>, as subst. <a data-ref=\"II Kings 6:32\" href=\"/II_Kings.6.32\">2 K 6:32</a> <em>murderer, assassin;</em> pl. <span dir=\"rtl\">מְרַצְּחִים</span> <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 1:21\" href=\"/Isaiah.1.21\">Is 1:21</a> <em>assassins</em>."}],"form":"Pi."},{"senses":[{"definition":"Impf., 2 mpl. <span dir=\"rtl\">תְּרָצְּחוּ</span> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 62:4\" href=\"/Psalms.62.4\">ψ 62:4</a>, so Baer Gi, van d. H. <span dir=\"rtl\">תְּרָצְהוּ</span>, but Ben Napht. <strong>Pi.</strong> <span dir=\"rtl\">תְּרַצְּחוּ</span> (Baer <sup>143</sup>), so Vrss Hup-Now De Che Bae al. <em>ye murder</em> (or <em>batter, shatter</em>)."}],"form":"Pu."}]},"rid":"BDB09513","strong_numbers":["7523"],"next_hw":"רֶ֫צַח","prev_hw":"תִּרְצָה","all_cited":true,"root":true,"quotes":[],"GK":["8357"],"TWOT":["2208"],"parent_lexicon_details":{"name":"BDB Dictionary","language":"heb.biblical","to_language":"eng","text_categories":[],"source":"BDB Dictionary","attribution":"F. Brown, S. Driver & C. Briggs","index_title":"BDB","version_title":"A Hebrew and English lexicon of the Old Testament, by Francis Brown. With the co-operation of S. R. Driver and Charles A. Briggs. Oxford, 1906","version_lang":"en","should_autocomplete":true}}